    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d907">

                <pb facs="0979" n="969" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg969"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">661.9331/10–749: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Tientsin</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Smyth</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tientsin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-10-07T13:00:00+08:00">October 7, 1949—1
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 9—7:17 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>823. … Machinery now arriving in Mukden from Russia, in return for soya beans
                    under barter agreement with Chinese Communists, is same machinery taken away
                    from Manchuria by Russians in 1945. Engineer, who is familiar with machinery,
                    says it is packed in same boxes as when taken away.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smyth</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
